Package: xemu
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: emulators for Commodore and Hungarian 8-bit computers
 Xemu ("X-Emulators") is LGB's suite of emulators for a set of mostly
 Commodore and Hungarian 8-bit machines, built on a shared SDL2 core. It
 is the reference emulator for several machines that are otherwise poorly
 served, including the Commodore 65 prototype and the MEGA65.
 .
 This package ships seven emulators:
 .
   * xc65      Commodore 65 / C64DX prototype (CSG 4510 CPU)
   * xmega65   MEGA65 (45GS02 CPU)
   * xclcd     Commodore LCD prototype
   * xvic20    Commodore VIC-20
   * xep128    Enterprise 64/128
   * xprimo    Primo
   * xtvc      Videoton TV Computer
 .
 No ROM images are bundled — supply your own, so the package carries no
 redistribution concerns.
 .
 The C65 and MEGA65 emulators are of particular interest for 65CE02 and
 45GS02 toolchain work: xc65 loads any 128 KiB file as its system ROM
 without validating it, so it doubles as a bare-metal execution
 environment for compiler output.
 .
 Note that an unrelated original-Xbox emulator is also called "xemu"
 (https://xemu.app). This package is LGB's 8-bit suite, which has shipped
 its own .deb under the name "xemu" since 2016.
